    "body": "## Summary\n\n`AbsorbedMLASelfAttention` is documented as mathematically equivalent to `MultiLatentAttention`, but its `__init__` computed `softmax_scale` as always `mscale * mscale * (1 / sqrt(q_head_dim))`, ignoring an explicit `config.softmax_scale` override. `MultiLatentAttention` itself checks for the override and uses it when present (e.g. the value `TransformerConfig.__post_init__` derives for muP training).\n\nWith muP enabled, this silently produces a different (and substantially larger, ~11x in the case checked) softmax scale on `AbsorbedMLA` than on standard `MLA`, despite the \"equivalent\" claim in the docstring.\n\n## Fix\n\nMirror `MultiLatentAttention`'s exact expression in `AbsorbedMLASelfAttention.__init__`:\n\n```python\nself.softmax_scale = (\n    mscale\n    * mscale\n    * (\n        (1 / math.sqrt(self.q_head_dim))\n        if self.config.softmax_scale is None\n        else self.config.softmax_scale\n    )\n)\n```\n\n## Test plan\n\nAdded `test_softmax_scale_respects_explicit_config_override` in `tests/unit_tests/transformer/experimental_attention_variant/test_absorbed_mla.py`, which builds both `AbsorbedMLASelfAttention` and `MLASelfAttention` from the same config with an explicit `softmax_scale` override and asserts the two match.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
